{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/138345-ideas-for-building-a-character","id":138345,"title":"Ideas for building a character!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-15T13:06:23-07:00","id":138345,"title":"Ideas for building a character!","content":"Hello forumites! So, I'm trying to build a character for a C:tL game, and I've decided to try to go for a 'inspiring general' motif. He'll be a Fairest Minstrel known for his battle cries, Dual Kith'ing into Flamesiren for an attachment to fire. Now, I've already picked out Enchanting Performance and Siren Song (both from RoS) to represent being a battle-herald. What sort of other things would you suggest for making him better at socializing and especially songs/performances? We start with a nice bit of XP and it looks to be a long term game, so I'd love to have some suggestions how I could advance him over time! Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3024-granitefarm","name":"granitefarm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T20:25:03-07:00","id":138806,"title":"","content":"Consider looking into Arcadian Body for Presence (though you'll have to determine whether it's worth the cost for yourself). A Goblin Vow with song, speech, or banners might lead to interesting results. Rigid Mask could help morale (&quot;We're definitely not screwed!&quot;). By way of normal Merits, look into Inspiring for more, uh... inspiringness. Depending on the size of your force, Small Unit Tactics from Dogs of War could be useful. Sworn Officer, Decorated, and Striking Looks could all be useful, though the latter is less distinctly so unless you've got an... unusual company.<br /> <br /> And of course you'll want combat capability, whether that be Hedge Dueling or a standard fighting style.<br /> <br /> I'd actually advise against Siren's Song, since it affects your allies as well (you cry out to inspire your people and they all take a -2 to all actions.))<br /> <br /> You'll definitely want Vainglory for the talkiness, and likely Contracts of the Board to serve as general. <br /> <br /> Talk to the ST and see if Elements (Air) or Elements (Sound) can be used to help amplify your voice.<br /> <br /> As a General I'm guessing you're Summer Court? Punishing Summer is great all-round for combat. Fleeting Summer can be used to address morale in a &quot;get angry at the enemy&quot; sort of way.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, it's just a matter of whether a given Contract clause or list will benefit your usual style of play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}